; Husky — AnimalDefinition data entry (gdd.md -> Data Schemas / Content Architecture).
; Roster row: roster.md -> Already-Defined Roster | Ruled: decisions.md -> D-43.
; Asset: Quaternius "Ultimate Animated Animal Pack", CC0 1.0 Universal — see
;   project/attribution/sources/quaternius_ultimate_animated_animals.tres.
; Source: source-content/assets/Ultimate Animated Animals - July 2021/glTF/Husky.gltf
;
; SPECIES: domestic dog, Siberian husky breed (Canis lupus familiaris).
;
; AVOIDS: ruled in as row 9's second Avoids pair (D-43), the candidate art.md and roster.md
; already named — mutual and symmetric with Shiba Inu below. Both are domestic dogs, so the
; structural predation-graph check stays clean the same way it does for Rabbit <-> Fox.
; Personality split (Husky Bold, Shiba Inu Shy) matches each breed's documented real
; temperament (huskies outgoing/pack-social, Shiba Inu independent/reserved) and gives this
; second pair its own visibility hook, the job Fox's Shy does for the first pair.
;
; CAPACITY FIELDS (D-43): capacity_radius = 0 -> SENTINEL `CAPACITY_RADIUS_FOLLOWS_SCOUT`,
; meaning "equal to scout_radius" (8), not a radius of zero. tiles_per_individual = 2,
; max_individuals = 6. Farm-tolerant, "village dog" — house + open_grass habitat.
;
; fact_text is docs/content/cleared-pool-fact-cards.md § Husky's proposed line, transcribed
; verbatim — all four checklist steps PASS there.
;   "bred to be strong pullers ... help pull heavy loads and sleds" -> ADW Canis lupus
;   familiaris, "Behavior": "...pulling loads (huskies, St. Bernard's)..." (one clause
;   drawn from a longer breed-role list; other items in that list name banned words
;   directly — "hunting", "catching rats", "guarding" — and are not used here; see the
;   source file's banned-vocabulary note.)
; https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Canis_lupus_familiaris/
;
; news_reports intentionally empty — News Report pools for this pool are a separate, later
; purchase (not part of Content Pipeline step 4/5 for this dispatch).
;
; TIERS — RE-SPEC 2026-09-04 (habitat tiers).
;
; PROPOSAL, NOT A DECISION. Every divisor below is this design's own first-pass proposal
; awaiting human sign-off, per the project rule that all tuning values are the human's.
; Source: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-habitat-tiers-design.md § 9.
;
; PERSON CATEGORY, needing an actual person rather than an empty house: single tier
; "companion": `snow/6` `people/2` — a husky's cold-climate ecology, now genuinely
; distinguishing it from Pug and Shiba Inu, which both gate on a house instead.
;
; The legacy flat fields (habitat_needs / tiles_per_individual / max_individuals) are LEFT
; IN PLACE and are now inert: `effective_tiers()` prefers `tiers` when non-empty. They are
; retained so a rollback is a one-line edit rather than a re-authoring.
[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="AnimalDefinition" load_steps=7 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/definitions/animal_definition.gd" id="1_schema"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://assets/animals/husky/Husky.tscn" id="2_model"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/definitions/habitat_need.gd" id="3_need"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/definitions/habitat_tier.gd" id="4_tier"]

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="need_companion_snow"]
script = ExtResource("3_need")
tag = "snow"
radius = 0
tiles_per_individual = 6

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="need_companion_people"]
script = ExtResource("3_need")
tag = "people"
radius = 0
tiles_per_individual = 2

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="tier_companion"]
script = ExtResource("4_tier")
id = "companion"
needs = Array[Resource]([SubResource("need_companion_snow"), SubResource("need_companion_people")])
limits = Array[Resource]([])
max_individuals = 6
arrival_group_size = 1

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_schema")
id = "husky"
display_name = "Husky"
habitat_needs = Array[String](["house", "open_grass"])
personality = "Bold"
avoids = Array[String](["shiba_inu"])
farm_tolerant = true
scout_radius = 8
capacity_radius = 0
tiles_per_individual = 2
max_individuals = 6
tiers = Array[Resource]([SubResource("tier_companion")])
emits_tags = Array[String]([])
model_scenes = Array[PackedScene]([ExtResource("2_model")])
fact_text_pool = Array[String](["Huskies were bred to be strong pullers — people used them to help pull heavy loads and sleds."])
news_reports = Array[String]([])
